        "serverInfo": {
          "name": "opencu",
          "version": "0.6.0"
        },
        "instructions": "Control Android applications on the main display with the independent OpenCU engine. Read get_app_state before input. Use observed element indexes; request screenshots before coordinate input. Coordinates refer to the scaled full-display JPEG. Actions return updated state. Use run_actions for a short known sequence; its indexes refer to the state before the batch. Steps may wait locally with until (text, gone, app, stable). A new dialog, unexpected app switch, failed step or person activity stops the batch; inspect its final state, never replay. type_text and set_value support Unicode through accessibility without changing the keyboard. Verify actual results before reporting success. Input uses the main display and can change foreground only after 10 seconds without physical input. A physical touch or key during a call returns PERSON_ACTIVE: stop and ask the person, never retry automatically. Three physical volume-down presses within 1.5 seconds latch USER_STOPPED for this connection; never reconnect or retry without explicit permission. Reads remain available after Stop. Locked or screen-off phones refuse input without waking or unlocking. There is no agent desktop in milestone 1. Keep one connection per agent session and never operate the same app concurrently. Respect user authorization and host approval rules. OpenCU runs locally as shell, opens no port, and requires no account or particular agent identity."
      }
    },
